>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `prepare_rewrite_bundle`

``` hol4
simpLib.prepare_rewrite_arguments :
  simpLib.simpset -> thm list -> simpLib.simpset * thm list
simpLib.prepare_rewrite_bundle :
  simpLib.simpset -> thm list -> simpLib.rewrite_bundle
simpLib.rewrite_bundle_rules : simpLib.rewrite_bundle ->
  (thm * simpLib.rewrite_source list) list
simpLib.combine_rewrite_bundles :
  simpLib.rewrite_bundle list -> simpLib.rewrite_bundle
simpLib.install_rewrite_bundle : simpLib.rewrite_bundle ->
  (simpLib.rewrite_source * thm) list ->
  simpLib.simpset -> simpLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Prepares a theorem-list argument once, for use in several simplifier calls.

`prepare_rewrite_arguments ss ths` applies the directives in `ths` (such
as `simpLib.ExclX`, `SF` and `Split`) to `ss`, returning the resulting
simpset and the remaining theorems.

`prepare_rewrite_bundle ss ths` turns the theorems `ths`, which should
contain no directives, into rewrites using the rewrite maker of `ss`,
without adding them to `ss`. `install_rewrite_bundle bundle views ss` adds
them to `ss`, together with the views `views` (see
`simpLib.rewrite_views`). `rewrite_bundle_rules bundle` returns each
theorem of the bundle with the handles of the rewrites made from it.
`combine_rewrite_bundles` joins bundles.

The rewrites of a bundle are made only once: wherever it is installed,
bounded rewrites (`Once`, `Ntimes`) share one count of remaining uses.
`simpLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC_CHILD_FIRST_BOUND` takes a bundle already
installed in its simpset.

### Failure

`prepare_rewrite_arguments` fails if a directive fails.
`install_rewrite_bundle` fails if the bundle is already installed in the
simpset, and `combine_rewrite_bundles` if a bundle occurs twice. Views
whose source is not a rewrite of the bundle are ignored.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val (ss, ths) = simpLib.prepare_rewrite_arguments
     boolSimps.bool_ss
     [BoundedRewrites.Once boolTheory.AND_CLAUSES];
>>_ val bundle = simpLib.prepare_rewrite_bundle ss ths;
>>_ val ss' = simpLib.install_rewrite_bundle bundle [] ss;
>> simpLib.SIMP_CONV ss' [] “T ∧ p”;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.rewrite_source_handles`](#simpLib.rewrite_source_handles),
[`simpLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC`](#simpLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC).
